course: dictionary
lesson: 4306
title: Gritty: sand, grit and courage
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to find the right one. «Conjunctivitis makes the eye red, gritty and sticky.» Here gritty describes how the eye feels, as if tiny hard bits are in it. The context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: «An eraser is rubber or plastic mixed with a gritty powder.» The powder is made of tiny hard bits, so gritty means full of tiny hard bits here. Ask yourself: is the word describing a thing, or a person, or a story?
explain: Gritty can also describe a person who is brave and determined. This comes from the noun grit, which means courage and perseverance. When you see a word with a new meaning, swap in your idea and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Gritty means full of tiny hard bits, like sand or small stones.
fact: A gritty person is brave and determined, and does not give up when things are hard.
fact: A gritty story or film shows life in a hard, realistic way, including poverty, crime or difficult times.
fact: «Grit» is the noun, and it means courage and perseverance, as in «true grit».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Conjunctivitis makes the eye red, gritty and sticky.» What does gritty describe here? | *A feeling as if tiny hard bits are in the eye | A soft, smooth feeling | A very loud noise | A bright, shiny colour
exercise: «She was a gritty runner who never gave up, even in the rain.» What does gritty mean here? | Full of sand | Very quiet | Wet and muddy | *Brave and determined
exercise: «An eraser is rubber or plastic mixed with a gritty powder.» What kind of powder is it? | *Powder with tiny hard bits in it | Powder that is wet and sticky | Powder that glows in the dark | Powder that is sweet to taste
test: The climber showed true grit when the rope snapped, and she kept on climbing. What does grit mean here? | Pencil marks rubbed away | *Courage and determination | Small stones on a path | Wet weather
test: «Her gritty drama showed life on the poorest streets, with crime and hard times.» What does gritty mean here? | *Hard and realistic, showing difficult lives | Full of sand | Shiny and new | Cheerful and funny
exam: Jayden says gritty must always mean sandy. Is he right? | No, gritty is never used to describe a person | Yes, it always means sandy | Yes, but only in science lessons | *No, gritty can also describe a brave person or a hard, realistic story
